nd the fight to end period absenteeism."/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico?favicon.2vob68tjqpejf.ico" sizes="256x256" type="image/x-icon"/><meta name="next-size-adjust" content=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/0cz1d0mv5g_q7.js" noModule=""></script></head><body class="min-h-full flex flex-col"><div hidden=""><!--$--><!--/$--></div><div class="grain" aria-hidden="true"></div><header class=""><div class="wrap"><nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary"><a class="brand" aria-label="Fountain of Hope home" href="/"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path><path d="M12 6.5v-2M9.5 4.5h5"></path></svg></span><span><span class="name">Fountain of Hope</span><span class="sub">Garissa, Kenya · Est. 2017</span></span></a><div class="nav-links"><a href="/#topics">Topics</a><a href="/#about">Our story</a><a href="/#footer">Contact</a></div><button class="menu-btn" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6h18M3 12h18M3 18h18"></path></svg></button><a class="nav-cta" href="/#footer">Support our work</a></nav></div><div class="mobile-menu "><a href="/#topics">Topics<small>Real stories</small></a><a href="/#about">Our story<small>From the ground</small></a><a href="/#footer">Contact<small>Get in touch</small></a></div></header><main><section class="hero" id="top" aria-label="Menstrual health and girls&#x27; education in Garissa"><div class="slides" aria-hidden="true"><div class="slide on"><img alt="Menstrual health support keeping Garissa&#x27;s girls in school" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" sizes="100vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="hero-inner wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Fountain of Hope</a><span class="sep">/</span><a href="/#topics">Topics</a><span class="sep">/</span><span class="here">Topic 02</span></nav><div class="hero-kicker"><span style="color:#FF9CBE;font-weight:700">EDUCATION · GIRL-CHILD RETENTION</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Garissa County</span></div><h1>No girl should miss school because<!-- --> <em>she cannot afford a pad.</em></h1><p class="hero-sub">Across Garissa, a girl’s period is still one of the surest ways to lose her school days — or her dreams. Menstrual health support keeps her learning, and with her dignity intact.</p><div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn--pink" href="#story">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M19 12l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/#topics">All topics</a></div></div><div class="scroll-cue"><span class="line"></span>Scroll</div></section><section class="page-lead"><div class="wrap page-lead-inner"><p>Menstrual health is a school story as much as a health story. When a girl cannot afford a pad — or is shamed for her period — she stays home, falls behind, and too often drops out for good. Fountain of Hope works to close that gap with dignity kits, menstrual education and community advocacy that keeps Garissa’s girls in school and dreaming big.</p></div></section><section class="fn-section" id="story"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv fn-head"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">The story</span><h2 class="h2">Dignity in school, <em>day after day.</em></h2></div><p class="fn-intro">Real change for girls looks small and everyday: a reusable pad, a safe place to change, a lesson that says a period is not a shame. Together these little dignities keep a girl at her desk — and on her path.</p></div><div class="fn-editorial"><div class="rv fn-art"><img alt="Menstrual health support and girl-child education in Garissa" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" sizes="60vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fsanitary.jpg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div><div class="rv fn-side"><div class="fn-card"><div class="no">— The story —</div><h3>What missing school costs a girl.</h3><p>Each missed period during a menstruation means missed lessons, missed confidence, and missed chances. In a county where the boy:girl schooling gap is stubborn, periods are too often the reason a girl falls behind or leaves.</p><div class="fn-meta"><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path></svg><span><b class="bold">Girl-Child Education &amp; Retention</b> <!-- -->· Fountain of Hope pillar</span></div><div><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path></svg><span>Menstrual health support · dignity kits · school advocacy</span></div></div></div><div class="verify-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"></path></svg><span><b>Note for the team:</b> written from Fountain of Hope’s strategic plan and public reporting on girls’ education in Garissa. Confirm the specific photo/place with the team before publishing.</span></div></div></div></div></section><section class="discuss" id="discuss"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv discuss-nav"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">The discussion, unpacked</span><h2>Why periods decide <em>school days.</em></h2><p>The quiet crisis behind the dropouts, and the everyday fix that keeps a girl at her desk.</p></div><div class="rv discuss-body"><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">01</span> The hidden dropout</h3><p>Across Garissa,<!-- --> <strong>girls miss school simply because they cannot afford pads</strong> <!-- -->— or because they lack a safe place to manage their period. Missed days become missed years, and the girls most at risk of early marriage and dropout are the ones most likely to be pushed out of the classroom altogether.</p></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">02</span> Dignity kits and the lessons that last</h3><div class="dd-facts"><div class="fact"><div class="k">Reusable pads &amp; undergarments</div><div class="v">Dignity kits that let a girl manage her period with<!-- --> <b>dignity and confidence</b> — and keep coming back to class.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">Menstrual education</div><div class="v">Conversations that replace <b>shame with knowledge</b> — for girls and for the communities around them.</div></div><div class="fact"><div class="k">School advocacy</div><div class="v">Safe facilities and supportive attitudes that<!-- --> <b>normalize menstruation</b> as part of every school day.</div></div></div></div><div class="dd-quote"><span class="qmark">“</span><blockquote>For too long, girls have missed school not because they lacked intelligence, but because they lacked a pad.</blockquote><div class="who">Voices in girls’ education · Garissa</div></div><div class="dd-block"><h3><span class="num">03</span> A girl in school changes a county</h3><p>An educated girl is healthier, marries later, and raises children who attend school. Every day Fountain of Hope helps a girl stay at her desk is<!-- --> <strong>an investment in Garissa’s future</strong> — one period, one pad, one school year at a time.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="related" id="related"><div class="wrap"><div class="rel-head rv"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--paper">Keep exploring</span><h2 class="h2">More topics from <em>the field.</em></h2></div></div><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/okoamama-activity-05"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 01</div><h4>When a budget meeting is a life-saving meeting</h4><p>Garissa’s health executive and its budget-makers sit at one table to deliberate maternal and newborn health — and agree the way forward together.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" href="/topics/clean-water"><div class="rel-num">→ <!-- -->Topic 03</div><h4>Clean water, and the dignity it brings</h4><p>Water, sanitation and hygiene work that protects mothers, children and whole communities in one of Kenya’s driest counties.</p><span class="lnk">Read the story<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a class="rel rv" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--navy);border-color:var(--navy)" href="/"><div class="rel-num" style="color:#FF9CBE">All topics</div><h4 style="color:#fff">Back to the Fountain of Hope story</h4><p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.7)">Explore the full one-page story and every topic.</p><span class="lnk" style="color:#FF9CBE;margin-top:auto">Open the home page<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="rv cta-in"><span class="eyebrow">Support the work</span><h2>Stand with the women who <em>lead this change.</em></h2><p>Your support funds dignity kits, school supplies and menstrual education for Garissa’s girls.</p><div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn--pink" href="/#footer">Donate now<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20c-3.5-2.6-6-5.6-6-8.5C6 8.6 8.2 7 10 7c1.3 0 2 .8 2 .8S13.7 7 15 7c1.8 0 4 1.6 4 4.5 0 2.9-2.5 5.9-6 8.5Z"></path></svg></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/#footer">Partner with us</a></div></div></